# ── OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ── Lock files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Do not add lockfiles here. Once you install a stack, commit the
# `package-lock.json`, `yarn.lock` or `pnpm-lock.yaml` your package manager
# generates: `/ci` writes an install step that needs it.

# ── Environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# ── "Ai" tool config ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only the pointers this scaffold's own setup creates, ignored so no one's tool
# choice travels with the repo. Agents that read AGENTS.md need nothing here —
# that file is committed. Add an agent that wants a config file of its own, and
# its pointer goes here too (see docs/agent-setup.md, "Adding a new agent").
# Config your editor writes for you alone belongs in your global gitignore
# (`git config --global core.excludesFile`), not in a template everyone clones.
#
# Anchor every pointer with a leading slash. A pattern with no slash in it
# matches at any depth, so it would also ignore a real config of the same name
# under `.agents/` — and git reports nothing when `git add -A` skips it.
#
# `.claude/` holds Claude Code's skills pointer. `/CLAUDE.md` is not created by
# setup: it is ignored because Claude Code reads `AGENTS.md` only while no
# `CLAUDE.md` exists. Committed, one (from `/init`, say) would silently switch
# every clone's Claude Code away from `AGENTS.md`; kept local, it is the personal
# `@AGENTS.md` fallback docs/agent-setup.md describes for older versions.
.claude/
/CLAUDE.md

# ── Personal context ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your own state file and decision log. They accumulate a record of your work on
# your project, so they are yours and are never committed to the scaffold. Both
# are created on first use. The convention travels with the scaffold; the
# entries do not. (sessions-archive.md is ignored too, for anyone who keeps an
# older session log of their own beside the state file.)
context/sessions.md
context/decisions.md
context/sessions-archive.md

# ── Stack-specific ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Add entries here based on your active stack selection in docs/project-brief.md.
# The agent will update this section automatically.
#
# Common examples:
#   dist/                 ← Vite, Astro, React, Svelte build output
#   .astro/               ← Astro cache
#   _site/                ← Eleventy build output
#   coverage/             ← Jest coverage reports
#   tsconfig.tsbuildinfo  ← TypeScript incremental build info
